      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the concept of similar triangles. Two triangles are similar if their corresponding angles are equal and their corresponding sides are proportional. In this case, the ratio of the longest sides of the two triangles is equal to the ratio of their perimeters.\n\nGiven that the longest side of the smaller triangle is 10 cm and the longest side of the larger triangle is 25 cm, we can set up the following proportion:\n\n$\\frac{10}{25} = \\frac{8}{x}$\n\nwhere $x$ is the longest side of the smaller triangle. Solving for $x$, we get:\n\n$x = \\frac{8 \\times 25}{10} = 20$\n\nSo, the longest side of the smaller triangle is 20 cm. Now, we can find the perimeter of the smaller triangle by adding up its side lengths:\n\nPerimeter of smaller triangle = 8 cm + 8 cm + 20 cm = 36 cm\n\nSince the triangles are similar, their perimeters are proportional. Therefore, the perimeter of the larger triangle is:\n\nPerimeter of larger triangle = $36 \\times \\frac{25}{10} = 90$ cm\n\nSo, the perimeter of the larger triangle is $\\boxed{90}$ cm.",
